01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
Milk is a 2008 American biographical drama film based on the life of gay rights activist and politician Harvey Milk, who was the first
openly gay man to be elected to public office in California, as a member of the San Francisco Board of Supervisors.

12
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
Directed by Gus Van Sant and written by Dustin Lance Black, the film stars Sean Penn as
Milk, alongside Emile Hirsch, Josh Brolin, Diego Luna, and James Franco.

13
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:18,000
Attempts to put Milk's life to film followed a 1984 documentary of his life and the aftermath of his assassination, titled The Times of Harvey Milk, which was loosely based upon Randy Shilts's 1982 biography,
The Mayor of Castro Street (the film won the Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature for 1984, and was awarded Special Jury Prize at the first Sundance Film Festival, among other awards).

14
01:29:36,000 --> 01:29:42,000
Various scripts were considered in the early 1990s, but projects
fell through for different reasons, until 2007.

15
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Much of Milk was filmed on Castro Street and other locations in San
Francisco, including Milk's former storefront, Castro Camera.

16
01:42:24,000 --> 01:42:30,000
The film was released to critical acclaim and grossed $54 million worldwide.

17
01:48:48,000 --> 01:48:54,000
It earned numerous accolades from film critics and guilds for Penn's and Brolin's performances, Van Sant's directing, and Black's screenplay, it received eight Oscar
nominations at the 81st Academy Awards, including Best Picture and went on to win two: Best Actor for Penn and Best Original Screenplay for Black.

18
01:55:12,000 --> 01:55:18,000
The film explores themes of california, election campaign,
politics, homophobia, san francisco, california.

19
02:01:36,000 --> 02:01:42,000
The tone is emotional and intense.
